  "description": "What the daemon makes of a reading of ups.status, given what it made of the last (power: online, battery or low), the time of the last answer that said something (answered_ns: the daemon's start until one does), and dead_ns (15 s, upsmon's DEADTIME). status is the value upsd gave, or null when it gave none: no connection, no answer in time, an ERR, a line that says nothing. The value is split at each space, empty parts dropped, and its flags are compared byte for byte. It says something when it holds OL, OB or FSD: then answered is true, unreachable false, and next is low with FSD, or OB and LB together; battery with OB; online with OL; except that from low, only OL goes back, to online. Otherwise, while now_ns - answered_ns is less than dead_ns, next is power and unreachable false; past that, unreachable is true, and next is low from battery or low, online from online, as upsmon counts a UPS on battery it no longer hears critical.",
